<<<
The only idiomatic sense of mosily is for the most part (The goods are mostly sent abroad./Twentyseven millions, mosily fools). But it is often wrongly used for most, as in the quotation; see UNIDIOMATIC -LY.
===
The only idiomatic sense of *mostly* is for the most part *(The goods are mostly sent abroad./Twenty-seven millions, mostly fools).* But it is often wrongly used for *most*, as in the quotation; see ^^UNIDIOMATIC -LY^^.
>>>

